{"seq":17,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T02:22:52.719Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"adae3396d33b9d336f292a1de4b42c60e5ccee10f1f8ad467920d400c622a9cc","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here's the list for Kwame's account review. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and the Coastal notes Moss wrote. I also included your own PHL cutover note, which is a public file.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (Gulf Coast)**\n- **#4419** (open): the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. This is from Moss's Coastal cheat sheet. See the conflict below.\n- **PD-8841**: how Pemberline Dock handles chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B. Hector, the night dispatcher, raised it. Source: your 8 Dec cutover recap.\n- **No ticket number:** a CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map. It needed watching during the 04:00 shift change. Source: your cutover recap.\n- **No ticket number:** chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change. Moss's cheat sheet calls it the main friction point.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (Puget Sound)**\n- **Feature request #882:** warehouse managers asked for a bulk-clear button for departed barges. Source: Moss's cheat sheet.\n- **No ticket number:** the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. Source: Moss's cheat sheet.\n- **No ticket number:** a request for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift. Source: Moss's 2 Nov digest.\n- **#4419:** the 2 Nov digest says Kwame's port account logged this one for a barge slip 7 schedule sync. It names Driftmoor in the same bullet.\n\n**Conflict to check:** Moss's notes attach #4419 to two different issues. The cheat sheet puts it on PHL (the report timeout) and the 2 Nov digest puts it on Driftmoor (barge slip 7 sync). I couldn't tell which is right, so please confirm with Kwame or the ticket itself before the review. I haven't guessed.\n\n**Left out as Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark:** PD-4821 and #8812. Moss separated those from the PHL port items in the 18 May notes, and the #coastal-random thread ties #8812 to the retail account. I also left out the Saltmarsh items.\n\nNothing in #coastal-team or #coastal-random lists a ticket for either account. The list is only as complete as Moss's notes and those channels, so tickets that were never posted there won't appear."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
